From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:02:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v20-common: turn the notification LED on

config_deviceLightCapabilities was 0, which tells the framework the
device has no lights of any kind. The V20 has a tri-colour LED in the
front top bezel: PMI8994 qcom,leds@d000 with rgb_0/1/2, LPG driven, so
colour and breathing both work in hardware.

With 0 the LED stayed dark for notifications and for charging, and
hal_light_default was left probing an LED nothing used, which is where
its max_brightness/trigger sysfs denials come from.

11 = LIGHTS_RGB_NOTIFICATION_LED | LIGHTS_RGB_BATTERY_LED |
LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED.

Confirmed dark on hardware while charging before this change. If a V20
variant turns out not to have the LED populated, this belongs in the
per-device tree rather than v20-common.
---
 .../lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml          | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml
index b601e39..c24ab90 100644
--- a/overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay-lineage/lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -29,7 +29,12 @@
 
          For example, a device support pulsating, RGB notification and
          battery LEDs would set this config to 11. -->
-    <integer name="config_deviceLightCapabilities">0</integer>
+    <!-- The V20 has a tri-colour notification LED: PMI8994 qcom,leds@d000 with rgb_0/1/2, LPG
+         driven, so it does colour and breathing. This was 0, meaning "no lights at all", which left
+         the LED dark for notifications and for charging, and left hal_light_default probing an LED
+         nothing was configured to use (its max_brightness/trigger denials).
+         1 = LIGHTS_RGB_NOTIFICATION_LED, 2 = LIGHTS_RGB_BATTERY_LED, 8 = LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED. -->
+    <integer name="config_deviceLightCapabilities">11</integer>
 
     <!-- Whether device has a notch -->
     <bool name="config_haveNotch">true</bool>
